   "id": "gen3-gen4-swaps",
   "type": "swap",
   "title": "Other LS swaps: L33, LY6, L92/LS3, E38",
   "summary": "Owner builds and their gotchas.",
   "conf": "forum",
   "src": [
    {
     "label": "PT.net LM7 to L33",
     "url": "https://www.performancetrucks.net/forums/fuel-systems-210/lm7-l33-swap-517133/"
    },
    {
     "label": "PT.net LM7 to LY6",
     "url": "https://www.performancetrucks.net/forums/gmt-800-older-gm-general-discussion-130/lm7-ly6-swap-info-544147/"
    },
    {
     "label": "PT.net L92/LS3",
     "url": "https://www.performancetrucks.net/forums/gm-engine-exhaust-performance-21/need-help-l92-ls3-swap-544861/"
    },
    {
     "label": "PT.net E38 / 6L80",
     "url": "https://www.performancetrucks.net/forums/gm-drivetrain-suspension-22/has-anyone-figured-out-how-run-6l80e-gmt800-513705/"
    }
   ],
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "L33 (05–07 aluminum 5.3): an 03 owner was told it's \"a direct swap with no issues at all.\" Valley knock sensors, rear cam sensor and 24x reluctor (one poster wrongly claimed side sensors and was corrected). Slightly bigger injectors; tune if you use them."
    },
    {
     "text": "LY6 (Gen IV iron 6.0, 58x) into a '99.5: VVT delete, Lingenfelter 58x→24x module, knock-sensor extension harness, EV1→EV6 injector adapters, cable-driven 92 mm throttle body. Another owner says with the Lingenfelter module you don't need the cam extension harness; the LY6 knock-sensor plug also differs. Return to returnless: Corvette inline regulator."
    },
    {
     "text": "L92 converted to LS3 spec (AFM/VVT delete) in a 2002 Avalanche with a built 4L80E and an LPE TRG-002 box: died after about 15 minutes with no spark (LPE suspected the box was overheating). His plan: 24x crank reluctor and 1x cam. Advice: Gen IV blocks have no rear cam-sensor provision, so use a 1x front cam sprocket and the 6.2 front sensor (12576407 per Lingenfelter, as cited). The 5.3 sensor is \"way too long.\" The TRG-002 needs a 4x cam signal."
    },
    {
     "text": "E38/GMLAN conversion: \"Over 2 weeks working every day,\" \"isn't cost effective.\" That owner kept a 4L80E and got the A/C working."
    }
   ],
   "torque": null,
   "parts": []
